###### Article 2 Meaning and scope

1. The Penal Code drafted under this legislative authorisation law shall observe the constitutional principles and norms and the norms contained in international instruments that, in this matter, bind the Timorese State.
2. The authorisation has the following meaning and scope:
a) Construction of a criminal legal system aimed at the protection of legal interests essential to life in Timorese society and the reintegration of offenders therein;
b) Enshrine the principle of legality and the prohibition of analogy with regard to the application of criminal law, although with the possibility of applying law subsequent to the commission of the crime whenever it proves more favourable in the specific case;
c) Stipulate that exceptional or temporary laws apply to acts committed during their validity even if judged after the period of validity;
d) Establish norms that define the place and time of commission of the crime;
e) Enshrine the principle of territoriality for the application of Timorese criminal law, individualising the restrictions to such principle and the cases of application to situations occurring outside Timorese territory;
f) Regulate the general prerequisites of crime, equating omission to action, unless the intention of the law is otherwise, whenever the legal type of crime comprises a certain result and the agent has the duty to prevent it;

g) Make objective imputation dependent on the existence of a causal nexus between the conduct and the typical result;
h) Objective imputation shall depend on the verification of intent or negligence, defining the types of intent (direct, necessary and eventual) and the modalities of negligence (conscious and unconscious);
i) Provide that criminal liability for crimes provided for in the Penal Code is non-transferable and has as its sole agents natural persons, admitting situations of liability for acting on behalf of another and that special legislation may enshrine the criminal liability of legal persons;
j) Enshrine the non-imputability of minors under 16 years of age and the requirements for non-imputability by reason of mental disorder;
k) Admit the possibility of aggravation of the penalty whenever the agent's liability, at least on grounds of negligence, must encompass a result not included in the type;
l) Enshrine mistake as to circumstances as excluding intent and mistake as to unlawfulness as relevant to exclude culpability;
m) As regards the forms of crime, establish as a principle the non-punishability of preparatory acts, and the rule of punishment of attempt in intentional crimes punishable with more than 3 years' imprisonment;
n) Define the concept of attempt, the measure of its punishment, cases of impossible attempt, the relevance of voluntary desistance and subsequent repentance both in individual actions and in cases of participation;
o) Establish the forms of authorship, instigation or complicity and define the liability of participants in culpability and unlawfulness;
p) Provide for and define the prerequisites of situations of concurrence of crimes, concurrence of sanctions, concurrence of crime with another offence and concurrence of norms;

q) Establish the rules for punishment of concurrence of crimes, even when subsequently discovered, admitting the possibility that the cumulation may reach 30 years' imprisonment and 600 days' fine;
r) Define continued crime and the rules for its punishment with the penalty applicable to the most serious conduct;
s) Enshrine the causes of exclusion of unlawfulness and culpability, systematically distinguishing one from the other and defining the respective prerequisites for application;
t) Introduce a title relating to circumstances which, not forming part of the legal type, assume relevance in determining the agent's criminal liability;
u) Proceed to the enumeration of aggravating circumstances of a general nature and to the enumeration of mitigating circumstances;
v) Provide for a general clause of extraordinary mitigation in addition to the special cases provided for in the law and delimit the respective consequences in determining the penal framework, through a model of degrees of mitigation;
w) As general modifying aggravating circumstances, enshrine recidivism and criminal habituality, providing for the respective prerequisites and consequences in the domain of penalty;
x) Construct a system of penalties and security measures whose difference is based on the capacity or not for culpability of the agent of the act; in the first case the concrete penalty may never exceed the measure of culpability and in the second they must be based on the agent's dangerousness;
y) Set out the determining principles in the choice of penalty and security measure as well as the effects thereof and the counting of time of deprivation of liberty before conviction;
z) With regard to the execution of penalties and measures involving deprivation of liberty, provide for the possibility of benefit of conditional release and the regime for probation, always with the consent of the person concerned and with the other requirements to be enshrined in complementary legislation that may provide for the conditions of

execution of the prison sentence, the rights and duties of prisoners and the existence of open regimes;
aa) Create a system of criminal sanctions for those imputable based on the following principal penalties: imprisonment, fine, community service and admonition;
bb) The penalty of imprisonment with a minimum duration of 30 days and maximum of 30 years, with the possibility of being suspended in its execution whenever it is not applied in a measure exceeding 3 years and the requirements of prevention of future crimes do not require its enforcement, and may or may not be conditioned on compliance with certain duties and/or subject to supervision by reintegration services during the period of suspension;
cc) Regulate the possibility of modification of the suspension regime initially applied and its revocation if during the period of suspension the convicted person commits an intentional crime for which he is convicted with a prison sentence or in cases of intentional non-compliance with the duties to which he is subject;
dd) Enshrine a regime of substitution of prison sentences applied in a measure not exceeding 12 months by fine or community service, according to the circumstances, with the duty of the court to justify non-substitution when, being able to, it does not use such measure;
ee) Not make alternative imprisonment correspond to the substitute fine and, in case of unjustified non-payment thereof, impose enforcement of the initially applied imprisonment;
ff) Stipulate that the fine penalty shall always be fixed in time, at a minimum of 10 days and maximum of 360 days, in principle, and determine that each day of fine corresponds to an amount to be fixed between half a dollar and 200 dollars, to be fixed according to the economic and financial situation of the convicted person;
gg) Whenever a fine penalty is directly applied, stipulate the duty to make alternative imprisonment correspond thereto for the corresponding time reduced to 2/3, as well as the possibility of payment of the fine in instalments, its reduction or exemption in cases of great

supervening difficulty or impossibility of compliance therewith;
hh) Provide for the possibility of the penalty of community service being able to substitute both imprisonment and fine in situations of minor and medium criminality and establish some of the conditions for its application and execution in coordination with reintegration services, as well as cases of exemption or reduction, leaving to complementary law the regulation of the other conditions of application and operation of this penalty;
ii) Enshrine the penalty of admonition for cases not punishable with abstract prison sentence exceeding 3 years provided that, cumulatively, reparation of the damage is verified, the agent is a first-time offender and the needs of prevention and rehabilitation are satisfied with admonition;
jj) Establish a system of accessory penalties, making certain crimes correspond to the prohibition of exercise of rights and professions, namely temporary suspension from public functions, prohibition of exercise of function, prohibition of driving, revocation of weapon carrying licence and expulsion of foreigners; such accessory penalties shall not operate automatically, depending on the prior application of a principal penalty and their duration variable with the measure of culpability;
kk) For those declared non-imputable by virtue of mental disorder, enshrine the possibility of application of security measures, of limited temporal duration, namely internment whenever reasons of dangerousness so advise and the obligation for the same to cease when the state that legitimised it ends, admitting that in the case of foreigners it may be replaced by expulsion;
ll) Also provide for the existence of measures of professional interdiction, licence revocation and prohibition of driving for those non-imputable by reason of mental disorder;
mm) Create an autonomous chapter relating to the matter of determination of the concrete penalty, both imprisonment and fine, setting out the general principles and the operations necessary for its choice and quantification;

nn) Stipulate that compensation for losses and damages arising from the commission of a crime, as to prerequisites and calculation, is governed by the norms of civil law but, unless otherwise declared by the injured party, shall be officially awarded by the court in the criminal proceedings and that the resulting credit is privileged;
oo) Determine the conditions for the loss of objects and advantages consequent upon a crime to be decreed by the court;
pp) Define for purposes of exercise of the right of complaint crimes as public or semi-public, identify the holders of that right, the time limit for its exercise and the conditions of waiver or withdrawal thereof;
qq) With regard to the extinction of criminal liability, fix the limitation periods for criminal proceedings taking into consideration the different frameworks of the type of crimes, the form of counting and the causes of suspension of limitation;
rr) Fix the limitation periods for penalties, security measures and accessory penalties, as well as situations of suspension thereof;
ss) Regulate the other cases of extinction of liability such as the death of the agent, amnesty, general pardon and pardon;
tt) Enshrine the imprescriptibility of criminal proceedings and penalties for the commission of war crimes, crimes against peace, humanity and freedom;
uu) Organise the special part of the Penal Code, Book Two, grouping the types of crimes according to the protected legal interests, creating Titles and Chapters as homogeneous as possible;
vv) In Title I, group the unlawful acts concerning crimes of Genocide and against Humanity, War crimes, including the prohibitive conducts of certain methods and means referenced in international law, war crimes against property and against goods protected by distinctive insignia or emblems or other rights and, still in this Title, the so-called crimes against Peace and Freedom, namely prohibiting incitement to war, acts of racial or religious discrimination, trafficking and slavery of persons and enshrining a legal type of crime that encompasses situations of terrorism;

ww) Still in Title I of the Special Part, the future Penal Code of Timor-Leste must take into account the international obligations assumed by the Country upon subscribing to and ratifying the Statute of the International Criminal Court;
xx) In Title II of the Special Part of the Code, eminently personal legal interests shall be protected, highlighting life, physical integrity, personal freedom, honour and protection of private life;
yy) Structure the protection of the legal interest of life through the imposition of differentiated penal frameworks according to the type of culpability of the agent (intent and negligence) and the qualifying circumstances of the greater or lesser degree of censurability, namely according to motives, the quality of the victim and the means and methods used to carry out the criminal design;
zz) Enshrine the protection of uterine life; provide for the privileging of infanticidal conduct by the parturient to restrictive cases occurring during childbirth, due to the disturbing influence thereof; criminalise incitement to suicide and situations of intentional abandonment or exposure of another that places their life in danger;
aaa) Define a set of incriminating norms that prohibit conduct violating the physical integrity of another person, graduating the abstract penal framework based on the degree of unlawfulness and the agent's culpability manifested in the seriousness of the injury, the type of culpability and the possibility or not of a certain result that exceeds the formulated criminal design still supporting imputation, at least on grounds of negligence, what doctrine calls aggravation by result;
bbb) Distinguish the incrimination of offences by means of poisonous substances, reciprocal offences and participation in affray with two or more persons;
ccc) Finally, still within the scope of bodily offences, implement two legal types of crime that specifically provide for the punishment of ill-treatment of minors or incapable persons and of spouses or those cohabiting in an analogous situation;

ddd) In the chapter on protection of personal freedom, criminalise conduct traditionally and at the level of comparative law integrating the types of crime of threats, coercion, kidnapping, abduction and other acts violating individual freedom and, specifically, create the type of unlawful act relating to the sale of persons and the omission of denunciation of situations capable of constituting the crimes in question;
eee) Enshrine a chapter relating to sexual criminality highlighting the legal interest of freedom in this domain as determinant of the conduct to be criminalised, protecting the youngest from acts for which they are not yet prepared to consciously decide in freedom, incriminate conduct revealing sexual exploitation and the most common forms of sexual abuse whether through fraud or by reason of age;
fff) In a very particular way, incriminate the practices of sexual prostitution, child pornography and any acts of a sexual nature with minors under twelve years of age;
ggg) Introduce the criminalisation of violation of secrecy, violation of domicile and other places and violation of correspondence and telecommunications;
hhh) Group in a single title a set of crimes that protect legal interests relating to public peace and tranquillity, State security, life in society, against public authority and within the scope of electoral activities;
iii) With regard to the domain of conduct capable of violating public peace and tranquillity, prevent the emergence of criminal associations, public attitudes of instigation to the commission of crimes, participation in public riots, behaviour that prevents the exercise of political rights by citizens, disobedience to the lawful order of dispersal, criminalise practices constituting influence peddling and punish the abuse of public signs or uniforms;

jjj) Within the scope of internal State security, provide for incriminating norms for conduct capable of putting it at risk in a more significant way, namely enshrining the legal type of crime of treason to the Homeland, collaboration with enemy armed forces of the Timorese State, sabotage against national defence and campaign against the effort for peace in Timor-Leste, attack against the Head of State or other actions against constitutional bodies or conduct that pursues as an end the alteration of the Rule of Law, diplomatic infidelity, violation of State secrecy and outrage to Timorese national symbols;
kkk) Criminalise fraudulent behaviour in electoral activities regardless of who the agent is and the phase of the electoral process, cases of obstruction of the exercise of candidacy or its unlawful exercise, situations of electoral propaganda in violation of the respective legal framework and actions that disturb the normal course of the electoral act;
lll) Life in modern societies develops in constant contact with conduct potentially generating dangers more or less close to materialisation and capable of violating interests whose integrity it is important to safeguard, such as the activity of driving motor vehicles, use and possession of weapons and certain activities with relevance in the domain of citizen and public health, and some types of crimes in this matter should be provided for;
mmm) In the same way, conduct capable of violating religious values established in Timorese society should be criminalised, failure to comply with maintenance obligations and others in the domain of custody of minors, cases of social solidarity arising from situations of calamity, disaster or mandatory for certain professional activities;
nnn) Criminally sanction conduct that is unsustainably harmful to the environment, namely fauna, flora, natural habitats and resources of the Timorese subsoil;
ooo) Criminally sanction conduct that violates the exercise of public authority,

namely by means of acts of disobedience, obstruction, destruction, resistance or usurpation of public offices;
ppp) With regard to the exercise of the action of execution of penalties or measures involving deprivation of liberty, criminalise conduct that translates into removal of prisoners, escape, assistance thereto by an official and mutiny of prisoners;
qqq) As a form of protection of patrimonial legal interests, enshrine two chapters grouping crimes against property in one and crimes against patrimony in general in another;
rrr) Construct a normative system protecting property based on the legal types of crime most common in various criminal legislations such as theft, robbery, breach of trust and damage, structuring these types into simple and aggravated, considering the circumstances of value combined with the nature of the thing appropriated, the means and forms of action, violence, threats or coercion or any others capable of significantly increasing culpability or unlawfulness;
sss) Distinguish, still with regard to property, the norms typifying theft of use of vehicles, cases of violence after subtraction, usurpation of immovable property and alteration of landmarks, maintaining the incrimination of involuntary damage and defining the types of prohibited burning and fire as types of crime specifically of special damage by reason of the means and of danger in view of the consequences normally associated therewith;
ttt) Protect patrimony in general not only with the most usual incriminations in this matter such as fraud, extortion, receiving and bankruptcy or insolvency but, above all, bearing in mind the needs arising from new technologies in commerce and the responsibilities to be required of those who, managing goods or assets of others, do not conduct themselves adequately in that profession of administration, we refer to the crimes of computer fraud and the forms of harmful and abusive administration;

uuu) In modern and democratic societies, justice and its exercise are interests justifying the intervention of criminal protection, and punishment should be enshrined for falsity of procedural acts, forms of obstruction of jurisdictional activity, its non-exercise as denial of justice and violation of the respective secrecy;
vvv) Include incriminations relating to acts of bribery, prevarication by magistrate or official and by lawyer or public defender, as well as other activities of personal favouritism in the domain of justice, without forgetting the classic incriminations of false denunciation, simulation of crime and non-reporting;
www) In addition to the references contained in the last two numbers, conduct should be criminalised that in the exercise of public functions translates into situations of corruption, embezzlement, abuse of power or public force or economic participation in business by those exercising public offices or functions;
xxx) In an autonomous title, prevent through adequate incriminating norms, conduct of falsification of documents, technical notations, currency and sealed or stamped values, weights and measures, marks, stamps and seals, diversifying the respective punishments according to the nature, probative or fiduciary value and public use or destination of the falsified objects and provide for the possibility of seizure and loss of objects intended for the commission of these crimes;
yyy) Still in the same domain of the economy, incrimination should be made of acts that constitute tax fraud or situations of smuggling and customs evasion with regard to customs or border matters, in addition to maintaining criminal punishment of disobedience to the requisition of goods ordered by the government and conduct capable of disturbing, harming or preventing the performance of certain public acts such as public tender or judicial auction.
